{comment}
  A bare FRAME: the page's own content at the content tag, in one column of plain type, monochrome, light or dark as
  the visitor's system is set -- and nothing else: no header, footer, navigation, search or JavaScript, and none of
  the partials the other layouts add (analytics, experiments, personalization, the consent banner, chat). Named by a
  site's root directory, it draws every page of that site; a landing page ("Under construction") is its first use.
{endcomment}
{include:`layouts/bare.html.dtmpl`}
  {fill:content}{content}{endfill}
{endinclude}
